 "action_summary": "The front door refuses every request to change a file: 0 of the 60 edit and file-making requests of a frozen 32-task file set. Pull request #6602 adds sixteen file rows but cannot merge: the referee allows three new rows per change, its rows are selected by shared words and passed 13 of 96 requests with a wrong result, and its compiler change fails 15 of 51 existing world-binding tests on current main. This change adapts three of its rows, file.copy.v1, file.rename.v1 and file.line.appended.v1, to current main. Each row declares request_word_coverage: required, and the front door refuses, before anything is written, a request with a word the selected row does not account for. The compiler's writer rules (the destination is the one the sentence states; no input is taken from the world) become a contract a row opts into, so every row that existed before binds exactly as it did. Two defects of the append row, found by fresh instances, are fixed: a quoted line was appended with its quotation marks, and a sentence stating two lines had one of them dropped silently. Measured in a sandbox on this tree: the true-capability harness passes 2000 of 2000 fresh folders through the front door and fails three deliberate mutations; the frozen file set goes from 25 to 32 right with 0 wrong and no file changed in a run that was not right; the unified-model suite passes 137 of 137. Three rows, no model, no spend, no program started.",
